{"step_index":214,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:49:21Z","input_tokens":3918,"cache_read_tokens":454626,"output_tokens":4311,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe task is to generate Spider-Verse megacity textures. Upgrading a texture generation script to create `sv_skyscraper_facade.png` is the initial goal. The required texture details include architectural mullions, glowing room effects, comic rooftop accents, and a dark obsidian base, all to create a comic book aesthetic.\n\n\nFocusing on the architectural details for the megacity textures, specifically considering the reflective properties of glass panels on skyscrapers, which will be incorporated into the scene. Planning to generate neon signs with a cyberpunk aesthetic to be included in the environment.\n\nNext, I'm architecting a Python script to match a specific data schema and automatically process it to generate the environment. The primary focus is on ensuring 3D clearances, reflections, and rendering speed are within acceptable limits.\n\n\nThe banking angle's sign needs careful consideration; it appears a positive bank tilts inward, correlating with the curve's direction.  The script will automatically validate the relationship between the `curv_1pm` and `bank_deg` values in the banked points, ensuring consistency.  A coordinate system check confirms the level up vector's positive Z direction for shallow pitches.\n\n\nThe cross-product of the forward and right vectors reveals the expected Z-axis direction for banking; a positive Z indicates the right edge goes up in a left turn, and the left edge goes up in a right turn. Examining the relationship between curvature and bank degree signs will confirm the high side of banked sections; for a right turn and positive bank degree, the positive Z (high) side is unambiguously identified. This runtime check ensures accurate inward tilt for all banked curves.\n\n\nThe Euler angles, right, and up basis will be documented to ensure alignment between the 3D road surface and the car's bank roll to the millimeter. Analysis suggests a raytracing setup for wet asphalt will eliminate the unwanted white sun wedge. Setting the `specular_factor` on the sun light to zero, while maintaining specific material properties like specular IOR and roughness for the wet asphalt, should achieve the desired effect. This configuration should ensure that specular reflections on the road are rendered correctly without the problematic white wedge.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":"31"}},{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v6_sv_textures.py\"","Replacement":"\"    out_p = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"sv_paper_grain.png\\\")\\n    Image.fromarray(paper).save(out_p, optimize=True)\\n    print(\\\"Saved:\\\", out_p)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 5. sv_skyscraper_facade.png (1024 x 2048) & sv_neon_signs.png (1024 x 2048)\\n#    Nueva York 2099 x Neo-Monaco Comic Skyscraper Windows & Vertical Neon Signs\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef build_sv_city_textures():\\n    # A) Skyscraper Facade (1024 x 2048): dark obsidian-indigo comic glass + glowing halftone rooms\\n    W, H = 1024, 2048\\n    img = Image.new(\\\"RGB\\\", (W, H), (8, 8, 20))\\n    dr = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\\n    INK = (4, 4, 12)\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(1610)\\n\\n    cols, rows = 16, 48\\n    cw, ch = W // cols, H // rows\\n    palette = [\\n        (0, 232, 255),    # Electric Cyan\\n        (255, 34, 132),   # Spider-Verse Hot Magenta\\n        (255, 196, 38),   # Warm Comic Gold\\n        (132, 56, 255),   # 2099 Ultraviolet\\n        (255, 78, 54),    # Coral Crimson\\n        (220, 245, 255),  # Crisp White Studio\\n    ]\\n    for r in range(rows):\\n        # Mechanical dark setback floors every 12 stories with neon trim band\\n        if r % 12 == 0:\\n            dr.rectangle([0, r * ch, W, (r + 1) * ch], fill=(12, 10, 28), outline=INK, width=4)\\n            trim_c = (0, 238, 255) if (r // 12) % 2 == 0 else (255, 28, 118)\\n            dr.rectangle([0, r * ch + 6, W, r * ch + 16], fill=trim_c)\\n            continue\\n        for c in range(cols):\\n            x0, y0 = c * cw + 6, r * ch + 5\\n            x1, y1 = (c + 1) * cw - 6, (r + 1) * ch - 5\\n            roll = rng.random()\\n            if roll < 0.34:\\n                wcol = palette[int(rng.integers(0, len(palette)))]\\n                if rng.random() < 0.45:\\n                    wcol = tuple(int(v * 0.58) for v in wcol)\\n                dr.rectangle([x0, y0, x1, y1], fill=wcol, outline=INK, width=3)\\n                # Comic diagonal window blind / reflection slash\\n     \n<truncated 2646 bytes>","Target":"\"    out_p = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \\\"sv_paper_grain.png\\\")\\n    Image.fromarray(paper).save(out_p, optimize=True)\\n    print(\\\"Saved:\\\", out_p)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    build_sv_pit_garage()\\n    build_sv_ad_boards()\\n    build_sv_bigscreen()\\n    build_sv_markers_and_paper()\\n    print(\\\"V6 SPIDER-VERSE TEXTURES COMPLETE.\\\")\""}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python \\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v6_sv_textures.py\\\"; & \\\"D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe\\\" -b --python-expr \\\"import bpy; l=bpy.data.lights.new('S','SUN'); print('Sun attrs:', hasattr(l,'specular_factor'), hasattr(l,'diffuse_factor'))\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolSummary":"\"Generate megacity textures and check Blender 5.3 Sun specular_factor\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
